    "role": "user",
    "content": "Program: CBTRN02C. Input files and their record layouts:\n\nDALYTRAN: CVTRA06Y DALYTRAN-RECORD (350 bytes)\n  DALYTRAN-ID                  X(16)\n  DALYTRAN-TYPE-CD             X(2)\n  DALYTRAN-CAT-CD              9(4)\n  DALYTRAN-SOURCE              X(10)\n  DALYTRAN-DESC                X(100)\n  DALYTRAN-AMT                 S9(9)V9(2)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-ID         9(9)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-NAME       X(50)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-CITY       X(50)\n  DALYTRAN-MERCHANT-ZIP        X(10)\n  DALYTRAN-CARD-NUM            X(16)\n  DALYTRAN-ORIG-TS             X(26)\n  DALYTRAN-PROC-TS             X(26)\n\nXREF: CVACT03Y CARD-XREF-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  XREF-CARD-NUM                X(16)\n  XREF-CUST-ID                 9(9)\n  XREF-ACCT-ID                 9(11)\n\nACCOUNT: CVACT01Y ACCOUNT-RECORD (300 bytes)\n  ACCT-ID                      9(11)\n  ACCT-ACTIVE-STATUS           X(1)\n  ACCT-CURR-BAL                S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CREDIT-LIMIT            S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CASH-CREDIT-LIMIT       S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-OPEN-DATE               X(10)\n  ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE          X(10)\n  ACCT-REISSUE-DATE            X(10)\n  ACCT-CURR-CYC-CREDIT         S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-CURR-CYC-DEBIT          S9(10)V9(2)\n  ACCT-ADDR-ZIP                X(10)\n  ACCT-GROUP-ID                X(10)\n\nTCATBAL: CVTRA01Y TRAN-CAT-BAL-RECORD (50 bytes)\n  TRANCAT-ACCT-ID              9(11)\n  TRANCAT-TYPE-CD              X(2)\n  TRANCAT-CD                   9(4)\n  TRAN-CAT-BAL                 S9(9)V9(2)\n\nRule to test:\n{\n \"id\": \"BR-CBTRN02C-002\",\n \"title\": \"Reject a transaction whose cross-referenced account does not exist\",\n \"summary\": \"After the card is found, the program reads the account file using the account ID from the cross-reference record. If no account record is found, the transaction fails with reason 101 'ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND' and the credit-limit and expiration checks are skipped.\",\n \"given\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The card was found in the cross-reference file, so the failure reason is still 0 and the account lookup runs.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"0\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The account file is read using the 11-digit account ID taken from the cross-reference record.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"XREF-ACCT-ID\",\n    \"FD-ACCT-ID\",\n    \"ACCOUNT-RECORD\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  }\n ],\n \"when\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"No account record exists for that account ID (keyed read returns INVALID KEY).\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"ACCOUNT-RECORD\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  }\n ],\n \"then\": [\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The failure reason is set to 101 and the description to 'ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND'. Because the failure reason is no longer 0, the main loop adds 1 to the reject count and writes a reject record instead of posting the transaction.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON\",\n    \"WS-VALIDATION-FAIL-REASON-DESC\",\n    \"WS-REJECT-COUNT\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": [\n    \"101\",\n    \"ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"text\": \"The credit-limit and expiration checks are in the NOT INVALID KEY branch, so they run only when the account record is found.\",\n   \"fields\": [\n    \"ACCT-CREDIT-LIMIT\",\n    \"ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE\"\n   ],\n   \"literals\": []\n  }\n ]\n}"
